{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966802,"nonce":"u5RxeKBc2wVvo/8RSuKgI7GL6uo=","title":"PENDING_SUBTREE_REBUILDS holds raw LayoutNodeIds; a full tree build restarts the slotmap so","message":"`crate::stateful::PENDING_SUBTREE_REBUILDS` entries carry a raw\n`LayoutNodeId`. `RenderTree::build_element` starts a fresh\n`LayoutTree`, so ids restart from the same seed and an entry queued\nagainst the previous build names a live node in the new one.\n`node_exists` waves it through and its children replace that node's,\nwith content from the tree it came from.\n\nSymptom under `.blinc` hot reload: the reloaded literal painted\ncorrectly, then reverted to its old text one frame later, in the box\nthe new text had sized. Saving a second time cleared it, which is why\nit read as a caching bug. It is not: the glyph cache, the composite\ntextures and the incremental diff were all correct, verified headlessly\n(`crates/blinc_cn_dsl/tests/reload_incremental.rs`).\n\n**How it was found**: a `tracing::trace!` on `text_data.content` at the\npaint site in `blinc_app::context`, then running the app under a script\nthat edited the source mid-run. Two consecutive frames, one correct and\none reverted, with `Subtree rebuilds processed` logged between them.\nThat log line is the tell.\n\nFix: a process-global build epoch in `stateful.rs`, bumped by\n`build_element` before anything can queue, stamped on each entry, and\ncompared against the tree's own in\n`process_pending_subtree_rebuilds_routed`. Same family as\ngotcha event router layout id staleness — anything holding a\n`LayoutNodeId` across a build is suspect.\n\nAlso landed with it: the reload no longer sets `ws.render_tree = None`.\nThe diff carries the edit in, so scroll offsets and focus survive; only\nCSS needs a forced pass, since an edited rule changes no element hash.","files":null}]}